{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529468-trouble-with-combat","id":1529468,"title":"Trouble With Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-25T15:34:29-08:00","id":1529468,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Trouble With Combat","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> new-ish storyteller here. For the past few months, I've been running a changing breeds game, and for the most part, it's going well. The group consists of a Glass Walker hacker, a Gurahl face, and a were-spider mystic. The group is still at Rank One.<br /> The problem I've encountered is that the werespider never has anything to do in combat. He has no combat abilities or gifts, so he spends combat ineffectually swinging at the enemy with his spider appendages. He's shown no interest in learning combat abilities because he wants to play a pure mystic character. Which is all well and good, but I have not been able to find any useful combat gifts at his rank. I've searched through the relevant books and can't find anything. It's possible I missed something, however. I've also been toying around with the idea of having him find a fetish which gives some dice to Brawl, but I'm not sure if he would want that.<br /> My main question is, do you all know of fetishes or Gifts that could help me out? I would appreciate any help you can provide.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T16:06:09-08:00","id":1529470,"title":"","content":"You could spin webs (all werespiders can do this given blood) and bind spirits into them to make them talens and enhance their utility as traps, using other talens as guidelines for possible effects. That would play into the player's ambitions in utilizing only the spiritual corner. That would tend to rely on selecting the battlefields, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T18:39:36-08:00","id":1529481,"title":"","content":"Why does that PC need any help with combat at all? Is the player complaining about being ineffectual or being bored, or is it you that is bothered by it? If the player complaining about not having fun in combat because he chooses not to improve his character in that way, he needs to come up with the solution, not you. Although you can always collaborate with him on a solution. At the most, maybe give their opponents some minions that are more along his power level instead of at the power level of the other two PCs. Maybe those minions are like him not combat oriented people, but they bring other skills the other bad guys can use (they are the getaway drivers, accountants, hackers, love interests, snitches, etc. that the others need). That PC can go after them while the others go after the combat foes.<br /> <br /> If he's not complaining and having fun despite being useless in combat, don't worry about it. Instead of trying to &quot;fix&quot; the PC to fit your image of what a PC should be able to do, make sure he has other opportunities where he can shine where he is intending the character to be. Come up with plot hooks and scenes that make use of the area the PC is most interested in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T19:04:47-08:00","id":1529483,"title":"","content":"Black Fox has the right of it.<br /> <br /> The one thing I would point out though, is that &quot;pure mystic&quot; in WtA isn't really a thing. The spirit world is a living, breathing, primal place. There are spirits that will only cooperate if they are hunted and captured because that's their nature. Not &quot;fighting&quot; them would insult them. Fera handle mystic matters in a very hands-on fashion because of their nature and the animism of the setting.<br /> <br /> If you intend to highlight this, and the player is avoiding skills you think will be important as play goes on, it might be important to discuss this with the player. Basically if you two have different ideas of what a &quot;pure mystic&quot; in WtA looks like, you need to find common ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T20:31:20-08:00","id":1529486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529468-trouble-with-combat?p=1529481#post1529481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does that PC need any help with combat at all? Is the player complaining about being ineffectual or being bored, or is it you that is bothered by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I should have been clearer in my post. The player has expressed disappointment and boredom about his character's ineffectiveness during combat. He has said he wants to find a gift to help him in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T22:52:06-08:00","id":1529490,"title":"","content":"Regardless of Rank, combat Gifts are only as good as your character's existing combat ability. Gifts are meant to supplement your character to supernatural levels, not replace having mundane stats in the first place. There's no small handful of Gifts that aren't going to require decide base traits to actually use effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-25T23:00:08-08:00","id":1529491,"title":"","content":"Likewise, combat-based fetishes are the same, they still work off of your base combat stats, just adding some new effect. Hell, a bunch of them are literally just claw carvings. There's not really an equivalent that behaves like wands, scrolls, or spells in DnD/Pathfinder.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the only way to fix not being effective at combat is to start taking some kind of combat dots with exp, or just accept that he'll have to make up for not being useful in combat elsewhere. I do appreciate that WoD in general does make non-combat characters much more viable than other games, but for Werewolf especially, there's no getting around that you need to have <i>something</i> just because you're going to be fighting eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28155,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","user":"gh0st-fox","date":". 01-26-2024, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T01:19:38-08:00","id":1529494,"title":"","content":"What is their Affiliation and Aspect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T05:59:51-08:00","id":1529502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529468-trouble-with-combat?p=1529494#post1529494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is their Affiliation and Aspect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kumoti Viskr","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T13:24:30-08:00","id":1529517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CardassianArtistry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529468-trouble-with-combat?p=1529502#post1529502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kumoti Viskr</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a Kumoti Viskr player who is also very focused on her mystic development, but as others have said, Ananasi have some natural abilities that can help a lot in a combat encounter.<br /> Crawlerling form is one of the best scouting options ever. It's an insanely useful shape. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1519030-ananasi-s-web-and-other-bonds\">Webs </a>and venom are a very potent combination. Gifts like Cling or Shroud are really good for ambushes - and that's probably the main forte of Ananasi Viskr in a fight. Most spiders are ambush predators, but even hunting species use surprise bursts rather than long battles of attrition.<br /> <br /> They are very good if they have time to prep, but next to a Gurahl they probably don't look like much in a direct confrontation. Maybe the contrast contributes to the feeling of the player, because honestly, Pithus form is no joke either.<br /> <br /> So their main focus for fight encounters is to get the opponent into a disadvantage before the fight even started, and the heavy hitter of the group can clean up the (sometimes literally) wrapped package. Scout the situation, set up traps, use their webs and venom to immobilize, use their Rites to buff the group and bargain with Spirits for help.<br /> In a pinch situation when there is no time for prep, the tactic is usually to go into Pithus, grapple, bite, and web the opponent. That's usually really effective to take out extras while the tank is entertaining the boss - and once that's done, look for a way to use the environment against the main opponent.<br /> <br /> In terms of Gifts, there isn't really one that will boost their combat prowess to be on par with that of a Gurahl or Garou in Crinos. Mother's Touch is a neat one for support, though. A Grapple or Martial Arts specialization for Brawl is also very useful - jiu-jitsu with eight limbs is twice the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T15:07:07-08:00","id":1529522,"title":"","content":"Bonus lemons to lemonade option: maybe the player can channel their frustrations into a character motivation and make it a goal to develop a Spiritual Martial Art for Ananasi akin to the Stargazer's Kailindo or Mage's Do that aligns with their mystic outlook. That could be a fun long term plan to go alongside with your chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-26T17:56:41-08:00","id":1529531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CardassianArtistry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529468-trouble-with-combat?p=1529502#post1529502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kumoti Viskr</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of Gifts the most fun one there is Scent of Sweet Honey.....which makes combat more than a little difficult for most individuals...<br /> <br /> But with that combination you really should be concentrating on Rites.<br /> <br /> - Rite of Binding is invaluable when combating Spirits<br /> - Rite of Silence for all sorts of reasons<br /> - Studying the Great Web for getting intel on upcoming threats<br /> - Summon Paradox- Kick Spirits back over the Gaunlet or Ruin a Mages day.<br /> - Rite of the Questing Stone- lets you find enemys before they find you<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean your the Ananasi equivalent of a Theurge- you should be summoning Spirits and paying Chiminage to them for services, binding gafflings into Talens to use as spiritual ' grenades', trading services with Jagglings to be able to call them to your side when needed.......<br /> <br /> .......or worse comes to worse stay back a shoot stuff from cover ( a lot of your Gifts and Rites can help with this).<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T13:55:26-08:00","id":1529567,"title":"","content":"Well, thank you all for your suggestions. I talked with my player, laid out all the options, and he chose to go into spirit wrangling and talen creation. He has like 26 XP stashed away to really kit out his spider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28099-cardassianartistry","name":"CardassianArtistry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28099_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}